# NeoBench program entry.
#
# The first line of a file that is neither blank nor a comment may say
# what the file is for.  "program = name" makes the file an entry rather
# than a document: choosing it in Files starts that program instead of
# opening it, so a drawer can hold a program the way the start menu
# does.  The name is one of the desktop's own -- files, clock, monitor,
# about, preferences, neotext, vlc, neoshell -- and a file that names
# anything else, or that says nothing at all, opens in the reader as it
# always has.
#
# The clock is filed in the tools drawer because that is where the
# programs that read the machine are kept: the dial is a tool, and a
# drawer should be able to start it the way the start menu starts what
# it lists.  The menu does not list it -- the one row under the rule
# is Preferences -- so this drawer is the way to the dial rather than
# a second way to it.

program = clock
